{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#466","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#466","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#466\",\"parent_revision\":\"4b3d58612f6daf647c99865ac1035d78b9b6d2eaab739dc7d41ac2a2df040b0f\",\"root_revision\":\"4b3d58612f6daf647c99865ac1035d78b9b6d2eaab739dc7d41ac2a2df040b0f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nbacklog_core exposes only tools. MCP resources are the correct primitive for readable, addressable content. Backlog items are a natural fit: each is a file with a stable identifier (issue number or title slug).\\n\\nMCP clients that support resources can browse, subscribe, and read items without calling tools. This is a lower-friction access pattern for read-only consumers (e.g., a client that wants to render a backlog view).\\n\\nProposed resources:\\n- `backlog://index` \u2014 JSON list of all open items (title, priority, issue, plan) \u2014 static resource\\n- `backlog://item/{selector}` \u2014 full content of a single item; selector = issue number or title slug \u2014 resource template\\n- `backlog://item/{selector}/body` \u2014 raw GitHub issue body \u2014 resource template\\n\\nFiles affected: `.claude/skills/backlog/backlog_core/server.py`\\n\\nSource: FastMCP v3 docs `servers/resources.mdx` \u2014 `@mcp.resource(\\\"uri://pattern\\\")` and `@mcp.resource(\\\"uri://{param}\\\")` for resource templates.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | FastMCP v3 `@mcp.resource()` pattern | AVAILABLE | Item description cites servers/resources.mdx |\\n| 2 | Overlap with #513 | AVAILABLE | Both items propose backlog:// resources |\\n| 3 | `backlog_core/server.py` | AVAILABLE | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 verify #513 status first; merge or close duplicate before implementing.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. Low complexity. Additive MCP surface. Potential duplicate of #513.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- `backlog://index` resource returns JSON list of all open items (title, priority, issue, plan)\\n- `backlog://item/{selector}` resource template returns full content of a single item\\n- `backlog://item/{selector}/body` resource template returns raw GitHub issue body\\n- Resources registered via `@mcp.resource()` in `server.py`\\n- `uv run fastmcp list` shows resources in addition to tools\\n- Note: this item overlaps significantly with #513 ('Expose backlog items as MCP resources via backlog://{slug}') \u2014 may be duplicates or complementary.\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 add @mcp.resource() handlers\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an MCP client that supports resource browsing, I need backlog items exposed as MCP resources via a `backlog://` URI scheme so I can browse and read items without calling tools.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **expose backlog items and index as mcp resources in backlog_core** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: fastmcp-creator skill review of backlog_core/server.py\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1de39b77ed85904b75cc87311d0fbbc0c2f0f7d26cfbe56096f6e022414844d6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTCRyg\"}"}